    "id": "train-1573",
    "question": "Oliver is working out in a gym. On Monday he worked out for 4 hours, and the next day for 2 hours less. On Wednesday he decided to work out twice as much as on Monday. On Thursday the gym was closed, so Oliver needed to exercise at home which took twice as much time as on Tuesday. How many hours in total have Oliver worked out during these four days?",
    "gold": "18",
    "answer": "On Tuesday, Oliver worked out for 4 - 2 = <<4-2=2>>2 hours.\nOn Wednesday he decided to work out twice as much as on Monday, so for 2 * 4 = <<2*4=8>>8 hours.\nOn Thursday, at home, Oliver trained twice as much as on Tuesday, so for 2 * 2 = <<2*2=4>>4 hours.\nIn total Oliver trained for 4 + 2 + 8 + 4 = <<4+2+8+4=18>>18 hours.\n#### 18"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine the total number of hours Oliver worked out over the four days, we will calculate the hours for each day step by step.\n\n1. **Monday:**\n   Oliver worked out for 4 hours.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Monday} = 4 \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Tuesday:**\n   Oliver worked out for 2 hours less than on Monday.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Tuesday} = 4 \\text{ hours} - 2 \\text{ hours} = 2 \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Wednesday:**\n   Oliver worked out twice as much as on Monday.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Wednesday} = 2 \\times 4 \\text{ hours} = 8 \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Thursday:**\n   Oliver exercised at home for twice as much time as on Tuesday.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Thursday} = 2 \\times 2 \\text{ hours} = 4 \\text{ hours}\n   \\]\n\nNow, we sum the hours worked out over the four days:\n\\[\n\\text{Total} = \\text{Monday} + \\text{Tuesday} + \\text{Wednesday} + \\text{Thursday} = 4 \\text{ hours} + 2 \\text{ hours} + 8 \\text{ hours} + 4 \\text{ hours} = 18 \\text{ hours}\n\\]\n\nThus, the total number of hours Oliver worked out during these four days is \\(\\boxed{18}\\).",
